1. Open Task Scheduler: Press the Windows key, type Task Scheduler, and open the application.
2. Create a New Task: In the right-hand panel, click Create Task... to open the task creation window.
3. Configure General Settings: Give your task a name, and under security options, make sure to check Run with highest privileges.
4. Set the Trigger: Go to the Triggers tab, click New..., and set the task to begin At startup, then click OK.
5. Select the Program: Go to the Actions tab, click New..., browse to select the executable file or script you want to run, and click OK.
6. Save the Task: Click OK at the bottom of the Create Task window to save your new scheduled task.
